<title>ITALY: Further Italy bank rate declines seen in February.</title>
<headline>Further Italy bank rate declines seen in February.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Falls in Italian banks' interest rates are likely in February after an average 0.15 percent decline in January, the president of the Italian banking association (ABI) Tancredi Bianchi said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Bianchi made the comment after a meeting of the association's executive committee.</p>
<p>&quot;The decline will continue. We had a 0.15 point fall in January, we will see a little more in February,&quot; said Bianchi.</p>
<p>The Bank of Italy cut its discount rate by 75 basis points on January 21 to 6.75 percent, which led to some Italian banks cutting rates they charge on loans to customers.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsrooom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
